{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792947684,"nonce":"06IWY7fJvcwqkIlWEITbD5lnmKE=","message":"Decision: page agent (ash-7d 2026-10-25, from the source; no custom-named agent has been tested yet).\n- Ash gives `ash_host_agent(name, len, address)`: a page-thread service (`./\u003cname\u003e.mjs`, `start({memory, address, canvas})`) where the event loop is alive and a WebSocket can open to any wss:// URL with any subprotocol or query. It works only when the program's memory is shared: the wasm32-wasip1-threads build on a cross-origin-isolated page, so whatever serves the page (the Cloudflare Worker, and the session's own demo page server) must send COOP same-origin and COEP. This also constrains embedding the playground in the Rayzor landing page (an iframe needs the same isolation).\n- No generic ring: copy docs/wasm/window.md (header with magic/version/capacities/head/tail u32s, an event ring page to guest and a command ring guest to page, one writer and one reader each, records `kind | length \u003c\u003c 16`, never wrapping, pad record, dropped counter). Our frames are kind 1, payload one length-prefixed frame.\n- Waking a blocked fiber: `ash_host_watch(word, handler, context)` on the event head; the agent bumps it and adds to the returned wake word with Atomics.notify; hlwgpu does this with ash.Future (hlp_future_create/resolve).\n- Neither import is callable from Haxe: RayDE needs a small Rust wasm side module (allocate the block, ash_host_agent(\"rayde_session\"), ash_host_watch, natives send(bytes) and recv returning a Future of bytes). Template: hlwgpu crates/hl_xidl, IMPORTS.md and gpu-agent.mjs.\n- ash-7d is building a minimal ring-echo example (side module, shim .mjs taking its transport from the page, Haxe client), tested in headless Chrome, reusable as a library named rayde_session. RayDE then supplies the real shim (web/session/src/client.js: Yjs, IndexedDB, reconnect, sign-in) and a Channel over the ring. The direct-socket test is not needed.","files":null}]}